From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:27:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Support graph maps (rr:graphMap, rr:graph)

Graph maps were ignored (README; issue #47): every triple went to the
default graph. R2RML (11.1) puts the triples of a subject whose subject map
has graph maps in those graphs, and the triples of a predicate-object map in
the graphs of the subject map and of its own graph maps; rr:defaultGraph
is the default graph. RMLio/rml-test-cases RMLTC0006a, 0007b, 0007e-f,
0008a and 0009b (CSV, JSON, XML) test them.

doObjectMappings now evaluates the graph maps (constant, template,
reference) of the subject map and of each predicate-object map for each
iteration ($graphs, $predicateGraphs), and clean distributes the triples of
each node object over its graphs, as JSON-LD named graphs
(objectHelper.distributeGraphs). Test: graph maps.
